Boeing B-52 Stratofortress for PteroSim

Flight dynamics

Lee Elliott's FlightGear B-52F YASim configuration is distributed under the
GNU General Public License, version 2 or later. The original XML and licence
are in source/. The JSBSim adaptation is distributed under the same licence.
https://github.com/FGMEMBERS/B-52F/blob/344df48dcb8231742615ef5f17bfb5a24b06f9cf/B-52F-yasim.xml

The adaptation uses the source's wing geometry and incidence, empty weight,
engine positions and dry thrust, fuel tank positions and capacities, and
tandem undercarriage geometry. The JSBSim aerodynamic coefficients, inertia,
damper and spring rates, and thrust lapse are estimates. The default tank
fill is 40%. Landing gear, flaps and brakes respond to JSBSim properties.
The Manual stick pilot drives roll, pitch, yaw and all eight throttles.

Visual

"Boeing B-52 Stratofortress" by bohmerang is licensed under CC BY 4.0.
https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/boeing-b-52-stratofortress-38b0c64bd552431394efa8625d7f5144
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

The GLB is included as downloaded. Visual.xml positions this static mesh at
the empty centre of gravity. Its landing gear and control surfaces do not
animate. The visual depicts a later Stratofortress configuration, while the
flight dynamics use the B-52F data.
